# Web (`apps/web`)

## Structure

- `src/main.tsx` – entry point; `src/App.tsx` – root component
- `src/lib/` – framework-agnostic helpers (`api-client.ts` is the only place that calls `fetch`)
- `src/hooks/` – reusable hooks (`use-*.ts`)
- `src/components/` – shared presentational components
- `src/features/<feature>/` – feature-scoped components, hooks and API calls
- `src/styles/` – global CSS

## Rules

- Function components and hooks only; named exports (no default exports except where a tool requires it).
- Import app code via the `@/` alias (maps to `src/`); import shared contracts from `@umc/shared`.
- All HTTP calls go through `apiRequest` in `src/lib/api-client.ts`, typed with DTOs from `@umc/shared`. Requests use relative `/api` paths (proxied to the API by Vite in dev).
- Only `VITE_`-prefixed env vars reach the browser; declare them in `src/vite-env.d.ts` and `.env.example`. Never put secrets in them.
- Follow the Rules of Hooks; effects that fetch must handle cleanup via `AbortController`.
- Keep components accessible: semantic HTML, labelled inputs, `aria-live` for async status.
